From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:40:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] tools: libtool: pass every sanitizer option through to
 the link

libtool passes -fsanitize=* to the link but drops the sanitizers' other
options, -fsanitize-trap=* among them, which decide whether the link
adds a runtime and, under LTO, what the checks become. A library that
libtool links, built with -fsanitize=undefined
-fsanitize-trap=undefined, then failed to link for want of libubsan,
which the musl toolchain does not have, or linked calls into it.

Add a patch to libtool that passes every option starting with
-fsanitize through, as it does those starting with -fno-sanitize. The
patch is meant for libtool upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ...sanitizer-option-through-to-the-link.patch | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tools/libtool/patches/150-pass-every-sanitizer-option-through-to-the-link.patch

diff --git a/tools/libtool/patches/150-pass-every-sanitizer-option-through-to-the-link.patch b/tools/libtool/patches/150-pass-every-sanitizer-option-through-to-the-link.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7c78cc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/libtool/patches/150-pass-every-sanitizer-option-through-to-the-link.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] libtool: pass every sanitizer option through to the link
+
+libtool passes -fsanitize=* to the compiler driver that links, but drops
+the sanitizers' other options, such as -fsanitize-trap=* and
+-fsanitize-recover=*. Those decide what the link does: with
+-fsanitize=undefined alone, GCC links libubsan, while with
+-fsanitize-trap=undefined too it needs no runtime; and under LTO, GCC
+expands the checks at the link, as traps or as calls into the runtime,
+by the options on the link line. A library built with
+-fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined therefore failed to link
+for want of a libubsan the toolchain does not have, or linked calls into
+it.
+
+Pass every option that starts with -fsanitize through, as
+-fno-sanitize* already is.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/build-aux/ltmain.in
++++ b/build-aux/ltmain.in
+@@ -5562,7 +5562,8 @@
+       # -stdlib=*            select c++ std lib with clang
+       # -fdiagnostics-color* simply affects output
+       # -frecord-gcc-switches used to verify flags were respected
+-      # -fsanitize=*         Clang/GCC memory and address sanitizer
++      # -fsanitize*          Clang/GCC sanitizers, and their options that the link
++      #                      needs too, such as -fsanitize-trap=*
+       # -fno-sanitize*       Clang/GCC memory and address sanitizer
+       # -shared-libsan       Link with shared sanitizer runtimes (Clang)
+       # -static-libsan       Link with static sanitizer runtimes (Clang)
+@@ -5579,7 +5580,7 @@
+       -t[45]*|-txscale*|-p|-pg|--coverage|-fprofile-*|-F*|@*|-tp=*|--sysroot=*| \
+       -O*|-g*|-flto*|-fwhopr*|-fuse-linker-plugin|-fstack-protector*|-no-canonical-prefixes| \
+       -stdlib=*|-rtlib=*|--unwindlib=*| \
+-      -specs=*|-fsanitize=*|-fno-sanitize*|-shared-libsan|-static-libsan| \
++      -specs=*|-fsanitize*|-fno-sanitize*|-shared-libsan|-static-libsan| \
+       -ffile-prefix-map=*|-fdebug-prefix-map=*|-fmacro-prefix-map=*|-fprofile-prefix-map=*| \
+       -fdiagnostics-color*|-frecord-gcc-switches| \
+       -fuse-ld=*|-static-*|-fcilkplus|-Wa,*|-Werror|-Werror=*)
